  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mozambique Cyclone Freddy ACJR-2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KULIMA was founded in 1984 during the Civil War to create better conditions &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; resettlement for refugees. In 1995 KULIMA was legally recognized by the Min. of Justice to officially operate throughout the whole country. Its expertise is Emergency Aid (FSL, nutrition, WASH, RRD; incl. various Zambezi river-related floods), integrated Socio-Economic Dev, Food Security, Environment &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Natural Resources, Education &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Community Health; always with a focus on community empowerment and linking hum. to dev. (nexus).KULIMA cooperates w/ EU, IOM, (I)NGOs and embassies. It maintains a strong logistics and operational presence and has hundreds of employees &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; volunteers; all are experienced and trained. In all its provincial delegations, KULIMA has a network of volunteers and a very solid and appreciated rapid deployment capacity.
KULIMA, a national NGO duly established through its provincial delegations in Mozambique &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; with a strong presence in Zambezia, &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; particularly in the Namacurra &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Maganja da Costa districts, through its district offices supported by a vast network of volunteers, will lead direct implementation of the project reaching 100% of the target population. KULIMA will lead on community mobilization, identification, selection, registration &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; validationof beneficiaries &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; is responsible for the implementation of WASH, FSL and Protection interventions.
KULIMA is a member of theprovincial &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; district Emergency Operating Councils, and actively participates in the coordination meetings that are activatedwith the onset of the floods &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; cyclones in addition to being a member of the WASH, FS, Protection, Edu. &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; Shelter clusters.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 1991 Kulima was founded as a Mozambican NGO. It is the successor of the French NGO Bioforce, which had begun implementing rural development projects in Mozambique in 1985. At the moment Kulima is implementing different projects in the capital and in six provinces. Its general goal is to support projects of rural people, women above all, in their production activities, with the goal to increase food security.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KULIMA</narrative>
  </participating-org>
